# VideoPlatform frontend — environment variables.
#
# Vite only exposes variables that start with VITE_, and it bakes their values into the
# JavaScript at BUILD time. They are therefore PUBLIC: never put a secret here. Changing one
# on Vercel needs a redeploy before it takes effect.
#
# VITE_API_BASE_URL tells the browser where the Api lives. Pick ONE mode (details in README.md):
#
#   Mode A — same origin through the Vercel rewrite  (best when you have no custom domain)
#       Leave it EMPTY / unset, and put your Api's real host in the "/api/:path*" rewrite of vercel.json.
#
#   Mode B — direct to the Api  (best with a custom domain: app.example.com + api.example.com)
#       Set it to the Api's public HTTPS origin: no trailing slash, and no trailing "/api".
#       Example:  VITE_API_BASE_URL=https://api.example.com
#       The Api must then list this site's origin in Frontend__Origin (CORS).
#
# Local development (npm run dev) needs nothing: it talks to http://localhost:5000 by default.
VITE_API_BASE_URL=

# DEMO MODE (no backend): VITE_DEMO_MODE=true makes the site run with a fake Api inside the browser.
# The shipped .env.production already sets it. Optional extras:
#   VITE_DEMO_HLS_URL=https://your-host/stream/master.m3u8   (HLS stream played by every "Ready" demo video)
#   VITE_DEMO_SPEED=1                                         (>1 = faster fake processing; used by the tests)
